{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pulls/31","id":5177994804,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVkT2ec8AAAABNKHuNA","html_url":"https://github.com/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pull/31","diff_url":"https://github.com/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pull/31.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pull/31.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/issues/31","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pulls/31/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pulls/31/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/issues/31/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/statuses/d9f7ba807454657ea1cbbb5daad52e773f1171a8","number":31,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Set up the package, checks and CI","user":{"login":"Vijay021212","id":240779358,"node_id":"U_kgDODloAXg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240779358?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212","html_url":"https://github.com/Vijay021212","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vijay021212/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #1\n\n## Summary\n\nSets up the foundation every later issue builds on: the Python package, the four automatic checks (lint, format, strict types, tests with a 90% coverage gate), CI on Windows and Linux, and the pull request template that carries the self-review into every pull request. No agent features yet.\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `pyproject.toml` | Package metadata, hatchling build with the version read from `__init__.py`, dev tools, and the settings for ruff, mypy, pytest and coverage |\n| `uv.lock` | Exact versions of every package |\n| `.python-version` | Python 3.12 for local development |\n| `src/pr_review_agent/__init__.py`, `py.typed` | The package, its version, and the typed marker (FR-24) |\n| `tests/test_package.py` | The installed version matches the code; `py.typed` ships with the package |\n| `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | ruff, ruff format, mypy and pytest on Windows and Linux × Python 3.12 and 3.13; actions pinned to commit SHAs; read-only permissions; a single `CI passed` job for branch protection |\n| `.github/dependabot.yml` | Weekly grouped updates for the actions and `uv.lock` |\n| `.github/pull_request_template.md` | Summary, changes, self-review, tests and definition of done |\n| `.gitattributes` | LF line endings on every platform |\n| `LICENSE`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `README.md` | MIT licence, changelog, README outline with badges and development commands |\n| `docs/plan.md` v1.2 | Records mypy and Windows CI in #1 and the definition of done |\n| `docs/design.md`, `docs/adr/003-own-model-wrappers.md` | One code example wrapped to the 100-character limit by `ruff format` |\n\n## Self-review\n\n**Gaps:** Every \"Done when\" item in #1 is covered. Beyond the issue: mypy strict and Windows CI (recorded in the plan), Dependabot, and the `CI passed` job. The required status check on `main` is added once CI has run on this pull request.\n\n**Integration:** No runtime code yet. `ruff` is set to skip `experiments/`, which is a finished record of ADR-001 and not product code. `ruff format` also checks Python examples inside the Markdown docs, which caught the long line fixed here.\n\n**Code quality:** One source for the version, comments explain each tool setting, and the workflow uses least-privilege permissions with credentials not kept after checkout.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **Unit:** 2 tests, 100% branch coverage. The gate fails the run below 90%.\n- **Integration:** Not needed: there are no stages yet.\n- **Real run:** Not needed: nothing user-visible changes. All four checks were run locally on Windows with Python 3.12 and passed.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [x] The \"Done when\" in the issue is met (the template check is visible on this pull request)\n- [x] Unit tests cover the new behaviour, including edge cases and failures\n- [x] Integration tests updated if a stage or its wiring changed (none yet)\n- [x] Real run done and pasted, if the user-visible behaviour changed (no change)\n- [x] `ruff`, `mypy`, `pytest` and the coverage gate pass locally; CI results below\n- [x] Self-review written above\n- [x] Docs updated if behaviour changed\r\n","labels":[{"id":12973251121,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVkT2ec8AAAADBUQaMQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vijay021212/pr-review-agent/labels/setup","name":"setup","description":"Project tooling and CI","color":"c5def5","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-05T20:11:02Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T19:18:37Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T19:18:34Z","merged_at":"2026-11-09T19:18:34Z","merge_commit_sha":"4f0ea4a8af7bce5985797e0d3db0799161c047bf","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Vijay021212:1-project-setup","ref":"1-project-setup","repo":{"id":1447360121,"node_id":"R_kgDOVkT2eQ","name":"pr-review-agent","full_name":"Vijay021212/pr-review-agent","owner":{"login":"Vijay021212","id":240779358,"node_id":"U_kgDODloAXg","